<header><h1>The Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_vuilraith">The Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="devour"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Devour">Devour</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When an opponent&rsquo;s Infantry II is destroyed during combat, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and the opponent rolls for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture? A: Both happen&rdquo; both capture and resurrection apply.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot capture the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan PDS.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is a Hel-Titan a valid target for effects on non-structures, and can it produce?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It is a structure as well as a ground force, so the Vuil&rsquo;raith vortex, which needs a non-structure, can&rsquo;t take it.&rdquo; Devour also captures only non-structure units.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Units destroyed by <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> or <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> rolls are not destroyed during combat, and are not captured by <sc>Devour</sc>. Units destroyed by <a href="/R_anti_fighter_barrage"><sc>Anti&ndash;Fighter Barrage</sc></a> are destroyed during combat, and are captured.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Vuil&rsquo;raith Devour ability capture units destroyed by Space Cannon or Bombardment?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; those happen outside space and ground combat, so Devour doesn&rsquo;t see them; Anti-Fighter Barrage is part of combat and counts.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="amalgamation"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Amalgamation">Amalgamation</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player produces multiple units, their <sc>Amalgamation</sc> ability may be applied to each.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What are captured units good for, and how do Amalgamation and Riftmeld use them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each captured unit or token gives one unit.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player has captured their own units, they may use their <sc>Amalgamation</sc> ability when producing a unit of that type, even if they have no other units of that type in their reinforcements.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><sc>Amalgamation</sc> does not change the cost of the produced units, only the resources spent.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What are captured units good for, and how do Amalgamation and Riftmeld use them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;its printed cost still counts toward limits like Integrated Economy&rsquo;s.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player uses the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Integrated_Economy"><i>Integrated Economy</i></a> technology, <sc>Amalgamation</sc> will have no effect on the limit to the units they may build.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What are captured units good for, and how do Amalgamation and Riftmeld use them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;its printed cost still counts toward limits like Integrated Economy&rsquo;s.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player produces one fighter or infantry without spending resources for each captured fighter or infantry they spend.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What are captured units good for, and how do Amalgamation and Riftmeld use them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Each captured unit or token gives one unit, even fighters or infantry.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player has the <a href="/F_naalu">Naalu</a> or <a href="/F_yin">Yin</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, they may spend one resource for one fighter or infantry, but spend a captured unit instead of that resource, then get one additional fighter or infantry for no cost, which will not count toward their production limit.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A captured faction&ndash;specific unit counts as a unit of its base type; for example, a captured <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Embers_of_Muaat#War_Sun:~:text=Prototype%20War%20Sun">Prototype War Sun</a> counts as a war sun.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What are captured units good for, and how do Amalgamation and Riftmeld use them?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Any captured unit of the base type works, a Prototype War Sun counting as a war sun.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot produce a war sun using <sc>Amalgamation</sc> unless they own their war sun unit upgrade technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith produce a captured war sun without the War Sun technology?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No, by analogy with rulings on Mentak&rsquo;s Salvage Operations and Nekro war suns.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="riftmeld"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Riftmeld">Riftmeld</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The returned captured unit may belong to any player, regardless of whether that player owns the corresponding unit upgrade.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With Riftmeld, must the captured unit belong to a player who has the upgrade?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; any captured unit of the matching type lets you ignore that upgrade&rsquo;s prerequisites.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="crucible"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Crucible">Crucible</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Each gravity rift will still provide its usual +1 to each ship&rsquo;s move value.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a ship benefit from the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal promissory note, The Crucible &hellip;? A: Yes &hellip; the bonus would apply to all ships that can make it to the active system, including the bonuses from the promissory and the rift they are passing through.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do gravity rifts work &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A ship whose path moves out of or through a rift gets +1 move for that path, one per rift.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Crucible</i> will provide an additional +1 to each ship&rsquo;s move value, which will not increase if that ship moves through two or more gravity rifts.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do the Crucible note&rsquo;s +1 and a gravity rift&rsquo;s +1 stack, and can I use several end-of-turn abilities?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes to both: movement bonuses stack&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of no gravity rifts will apply +0 to its move value.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of two gravity rifts will apply +3 to its move value.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A ship that moves through or out of three gravity rifts will apply +4 to its move value.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>And so on.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a ship could move from its current system to the active system through a gravity rift if its move value were +2, it may do so using <i>Crucible</i>. This is true even if that ship could not reach the gravity rift without <i>Crucible</i>.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can a ship benefit from the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal promissory note, The Crucible, if it would not be able to reach a gravity rift on the way to the active system without it? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>For example, consider a series of systems X&ndash;S&ndash;G&ndash;Y. Only systems connected by a &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; are adjacent. System &ldquo;G&rdquo; is a gravity rift. Systems &ldquo;X&rdquo;, &ldquo;S&rdquo; and &ldquo;Y&rdquo; are standard systems with no movement restrictions. A ship with a move value of one is in system &ldquo;X&rdquo;. Were it to have +2 to its movement value, it could reach system &ldquo;Y&rdquo;. Currently, that ship may reach only system &ldquo;S&rdquo;. Despite this, if its owner activated system &ldquo;Y&rdquo; and played <i>Crucible</i>, the ship could move to that system.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;the bonus would apply to all ships that can make it to the active system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a player plays both <i>Crucible</i> and the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Nav%20Suite"><i>Nav Suite</i></a> action card during the same tactical action, they will still apply +1 to the move value of their ships that move through or out of a gravity rift.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This +1 comes from the effect of <i>Crucible</i>. The gravity rift itself does not give its +1 because of <i>Nav Suite</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="vortex"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Vortex">Vortex</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Vortex</i> cannot be used if there are no units that can be targeted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Vuil&rsquo;raith Vortex: &ldquo;Can Vortex be used on a ship if a player doesn&rsquo;t have any of those ships in their reinforcements? A: No, since they cannot fully resolve Vortex.&rdquo; Vortex cannot be used without a unit it can capture.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has all their units of a particular type on the board, other than fighters or infantry, that type of unit belonging to that player cannot be targeted.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Vuil&rsquo;raith Vortex: &ldquo;No, since they cannot fully resolve Vortex.&rdquo; cannot target if none in reinforcements.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If another player is blockading a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a>, their units cannot be targeted with <i>Vortex</i>.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Capture: &ldquo;If at least one of a player&rsquo;s space docks is being blockaded, they cannot capture units from the player who is blockading them.&rdquo; The Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s space docks are Dimensional Tears.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Vortex</i> cannot target the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s Hel Titan, as it is a structure.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is a Hel-Titan a valid target for effects on non-structures, and can it produce?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It is a structure as well as a ground force, so the Vuil&rsquo;raith vortex, which needs a non-structure, can&rsquo;t take it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dimensional-tear"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A system containing a Dimensional Tear is an anomaly.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Are systems that contain Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears anomalies? A: Yes, any game effect that references an anomaly includes systems containing Dimensional Tears.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Vuil&rsquo;raith ships roll for Cormund&rsquo;s gravity rift if their Dimensional Tear dock is there, and do two tears stack?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it is simply a gravity rift, and counts as an anomaly for objectives.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This system qualifies for the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Make%20History"><i>Make History</i></a> and similar such objectives.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do the Vuil&rsquo;raith roll for ordinary gravity rifts?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Those dock systems are anomalies, which counts for objectives like Making History.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a ship moves through or out of the same gravity rift multiple times, that gravity rift provides +1 to its move value only once, but the ship rolls for removal each time.<sup>6,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;If a player moves a ship through the same gravity rift multiple times in one action, do they still have to roll the dice multiple times?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes, although the movement bonus is once per ship per tactical action, the negative roll requirement remains per time a ship moves out of or through a gravity rift.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, Clarifications: &ldquo;A gravity rift can only contribute its movement bonus to ships that pass through it once per ship. This is a change from previous rulings.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Multiple Dimensional Tears in a single system have no additional effects.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Vuil&rsquo;raith ships roll for Cormund&rsquo;s gravity rift if their Dimensional Tear dock is there, and do two tears stack?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Two tears in one system don&rsquo;t stack the bonus either.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a Dimensional Tear is in a system that is normally a gravity rift (e.g. the Cormund system), the Vuil&rsquo;raith player will not have to roll for removal when moving out of or through that system. There are no additional effects.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Vuil&rsquo;raith ships roll for Cormund&rsquo;s gravity rift if their Dimensional Tear dock is there, and do two tears stack?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No roll: a system with more than one rift counts as one gravity rift, and Dimensional Tear says your ships don&rsquo;t roll for that system&rsquo;s rift.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has copied Dimensional Tear II, systems containing the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s space docks are gravity rifts for the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s ships. The Vuil&rsquo;raith player must roll for removal for each ship that moves out of or through those systems.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. RulesPal (NOT USED, unconfirmed), &ldquo;Do Nekro-copied Dimensional Tears affect the Vuil&rsquo;raith &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Tears only hinder other players&rsquo; units: Vuil&rsquo;raith ignore their own, Nekro ignore Nekro&rsquo;s, but Vuil&rsquo;raith are affected by Nekro tears.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a Dimensional Tear is in a system with a Nebula, then the +1 to move values will be applied after the nebula sets each ship&rsquo;s move value to 1.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Dimensional Tear plastic figure is destroyed, the Dimensional Tear token is also removed.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;If a space dock that has a dimensional tear token under it is destroyed, the dimensional tear token is removed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-terror-between"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Terror%20Between">The Terror Between</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When <i>The Terror Between</i> is destroyed, it still captures units that were destroyed at the same time.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does the Cabal Flagship capture other units that are destroyed in the same timing window in which it is destroyed? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does the Vuil&rsquo;raith flagship capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the Cabal flagship is destroyed too but still captures everything else destroyed there.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>Using the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability of units is done before remaining hits are assigned. As such, if <i>The Terror Between</i> is destroyed by a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card, units destroyed by being assigned hits in the same round of combat, or from the same pool of <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> hits, will not be captured.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If ships are destroyed outside of combat, those ships will still be captured by <i>The Terror Between</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;What does the Vuil&rsquo;raith flagship capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Every other non-structure unit destroyed in its system, the Cabal&rsquo;s own included, even outside combat: Bombardment, Space Cannon, action cards, agendas.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="the-stillness-of-stars"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=The%20Stillness%20of%20Stars">The Stillness of Stars</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player loses their commodities immediately after replenishing them, most commonly via that player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Trade_Agreement"><i>Trade Agreement</i></a> promissory note, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player may still target them. If they do, they still use that player&rsquo;s full commodity value to determine which units may be captured.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith Cabal use their agent on someone who has their Trade Agreement used to take their commodities? A: Yes, the commodities would not be there but the agent could still be used to capture a ship up to the player&rsquo;s commodity value.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot capture a unit without a cost. Notably, they cannot capture a PDS, a space dock, or a war sun of a player without their war sun unit upgrade.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player chooses to capture a fighter or infantry, they will capture one, not two.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How do you capture fighters and infantry?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A captured fighter or infantry goes back to its owner&rsquo;s reinforcements &hellip; and the captor places a matching token on their faction sheet instead.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the primary ability of the <a href="/R_trade"><i>Trade</i></a> strategy card is resolved, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player must choose if they will use The Stillness of Stars or not after the active player has replenished their commodities, but before players are chosen to perform the secondary ability without spending a command token.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When the secondary ability of the <a href="/R_trade"><i>Trade</i></a> strategy card is resolved, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player must choose if they will use The Stillness of Stars or not after the current player has replenished their commodities, but before the next player has decided if they will spend a command token to perform the secondary.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When The Stillness of Stars converts a player&rsquo;s commodities to trade goods, those trade goods are not treated as being gained for the purpose of triggering other abilities. In particular, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> faction ability is not triggered by this ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does Cabal Agent count as &lsquo;converting your own commodities&rsquo; &hellip;? A: No, whenever commodities are converted to a player&rsquo;s own trade good area, they are not considered gained.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="that-which-molds-flesh"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=That%20Which%20Molds%20Flesh">That Which Molds Flesh</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="it-feeds-on-carrion"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=It%20Feeds%20on%20Carrion">It Feeds on Carrion</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Anchor">Dimensional Anchor</a><sub> (Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Units captured while resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i> are not destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s units are blockading one of the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s Dimensional Tears, dice will not be rolled for that player&rsquo;s units when resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i>.<sup>8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook, Capture: &ldquo;If at least one of a player&rsquo;s space docks is being blockaded, they cannot capture units from the player who is blockading them.&rdquo; The Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s space docks are Dimensional Tears.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Each non&ndash;fighter ship affected will roll only once, regardless of how many Dimensional Tears it is adjacent to.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Vuil&rsquo;raith hero make a ship roll once per adjacent dimensional tear?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; each non-fighter ship in or next to a dimensional tear rolls once, however many tears it touches.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Units can only be captured by the dice specifically allocated to them.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ship with capacity is captured, its owner chooses which excess fighters and ground forces are removed; they are not assigned to particular ships.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 16.3: &ldquo;If a player has more fighters and ground forces in the space area of a system than the total capacity of that player&rsquo;s ships in that system, that player must remove the excess units.&rdquo; LRR 16.4: &ldquo;Fighters and ground forces are not assigned to specific ships, except while they are being transported.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player has used a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Valefar%20Assimilator"><i>Valefar Assimilator</i></a> faction technology to copy <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Dimensional%20Tear">Dimensional Tear</a> II, ships in systems containing or adjacent to the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s space docks will also have to roll for capture when resolving <i>Dimensional Anchor</i>. This includes the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s own ships.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="reanimator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Reanimator">Reanimator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player owns the Infantry II unit upgrade technology, and one is destroyed during ground combat on a planet with a Reanimator, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player captures an infantry token, and they roll for resurrection, placing the destroyed infantry on the Infantry II unit upgrade card if successful.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;What is the interaction between Infantry 2 and Capture? A: Both happen&rdquo; both capture and resurrection apply.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Vuil&rsquo;raith player&rsquo;s infantry on a planet with a Reanimator are destroyed outside of combat, such as with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Plague"><i>Plague</i></a> action card, those infantry will be captured.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="alraith-ix-ianovar"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Al%27raith%20Ix%20Ianovar">Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot choose to roll for The Fracture when they gain <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i>; the breakthrough&rsquo;s ability replaces the roll.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar (Breakthrough): Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith player choose to perform a breakthrough roll first? A: No, the breakthrough replaces the roll with its own ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When The Fracture is brought into play by <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i>, the Vuil&rsquo;raith player places ingress tokens according to the synergy on the Cabal breakthrough.<sup>6,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Since the Fracture enters play without a roll via Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar, do you place 6 ingress tokens, or just 4? A: Cabal BT will place Fracture as if it were rolled for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Cabal Breakthrough&rdquo;: &ldquo;According to cabal BT colors.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This uses the cabal breakthrough synergy colors method, not the one planet per color method.<sup>9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Cabal Breakthrough&rdquo;: &ldquo;should cabal place them according to cabal synergy &hellip;? A: According to cabal BT colors.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>When <i>Al&rsquo;raith Ix Ianovar</i> causes The Fracture to enter play, all the ingress tokens will be placed before the Vuil&rsquo;raith player chooses which tokens they wish to move into gravity rifts.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>The Vuil&rsquo;raith player may move the ingress tokens into systems that contain their Dimensional Tears.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>They cannot move an ingress token into a system that already contains an ingress token.<sup>6,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith player move an ingress token into a system that already contains a different ingress token? A: No, the rules state that a system may not contain more than 1 ingress token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, The Fracture: &ldquo;A system cannot have more than one ingress token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Ingress tokens cannot be placed in The Fracture. The Vuil&rsquo;raith player cannot move an ingress token into a system in The Fracture, even if they have a space dock in that system.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can the Vuil&rsquo;raith player move an ingress token into the Fracture by gaining their breakthrough after the Fracture is in play &hellip;? A: No, ingress tokens cannot be placed in the Fracture.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
